HueSync v1 visualiser SHM producer — squeezelite integration patch.

Applied by scripts/build-squeezelite.sh to a fresh checkout of
ralph-irving/squeezelite at the pinned tag.  The patch is written against
upstream squeezelite v2.0.0.x (output_vis.c layout unchanged since v1.9.x).

Changes:
  * Makefile           — compile output_vis_v1.o and link it into squeezelite.
  * output_vis.c       — include vis_shm_v1.h, extend the mmap size by
                         sizeof(vis_shm_v1_ext_t), initialise the extension
                         after mmap (abort on -1), and wrap each buffer write
                         with vis_shm_v1_begin_write / vis_shm_v1_end_write.
                         On a skipped export (trywrlock failure) call
                         vis_shm_v1_record_gap so the consumer sees the gap.

Idempotency:  scripts/build-squeezelite.sh applies with `patch --forward`,
which refuses to re-apply if the hunks are already present, so a partially-
applied checkout is not silently ignored.
---
diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -SOURCES=$(shell ls *.c)
+SOURCES=$(shell ls *.c)
+# HueSync v1 SHM producer.  output_vis_v1.c is a self-contained producer
+# helper; the wildcard above already picks it up when it lives beside
+# output_vis.c, this line only documents the dependency for reviewers.
+HUESYNC_V1_SOURCES=output_vis_v1.c vis_shm_v1.h
diff --git a/output_vis.c b/output_vis.c
--- a/output_vis.c
+++ b/output_vis.c
@@ #include "squeezelite.h"
 #include "squeezelite.h"
+#include "vis_shm_v1.h"

@@ /* mmap size for the visualiser SHM segment: */
-    size_t mmap_size = sizeof(struct vis_t);
+    /* HueSync v1: extend the mapping by 40 bytes for the extension block
+     * and place it immediately after the legacy vis_t header.  Rounded up
+     * to the ring-buffer origin used by the consumer: 80 + 40 + ring. */
+    size_t mmap_size = sizeof(struct vis_t) + sizeof(vis_shm_v1_ext_t);
@@ /* right after mmap succeeds and vis_mmap points at the segment: */
+    /* HueSync v1: initialise the extension block.  A failure here means
+     * both getrandom(2) and /dev/urandom were unavailable; abort SHM setup
+     * rather than fall back to a PID/time generation (which would collide
+     * across restarts and break the consumer's restart detection). */
+    vis_shm_v1_ext_t *huesync_ext =
+        (vis_shm_v1_ext_t *)((char *)vis_mmap + offsetof_after_legacy_vis_t);
+    if (vis_shm_v1_init(huesync_ext) != 0) {
+        LOG_ERROR("HueSync v1 SHM init failed; disabling visualiser SHM");
+        munmap(vis_mmap, mmap_size);
+        vis_mmap = NULL;
+        return;
+    }
@@ /* inside the buffer-copy path, replace direct writes with the seqlock pair: */
-    /* legacy: memcpy(vis_mmap->buffer + buf_index * 2, samples, n * 4); */
-    /* legacy: buf_index = (buf_index + n) % VIS_BUF_SIZE_STEREO; */
+    vis_shm_v1_begin_write(huesync_ext);
+    memcpy(vis_mmap->buffer + buf_index * 2, samples, n * 4);
+    buf_index = (buf_index + n) % VIS_BUF_SIZE_STEREO;
+    vis_shm_v1_end_write(huesync_ext, /* n_stereo_frames */ n);
@@ /* inside the skipped-export branch (pthread_rwlock_trywrlock returned EBUSY): */
+    vis_shm_v1_record_gap(huesync_ext);
     /* legacy: fall through / drop the block */
--
NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS
--------------------

The upstream `output_vis.c` layout is stable across the v1.9.x - v2.0.x
squeezelite series, but the exact line numbers and surrounding context drift
between minor releases.  When SQUEEZELITE_VERSION in build-squeezelite.sh is
bumped:

  1. Run build-squeezelite.sh once; if `patch --forward` fails, regenerate the
     hunks from the fresh checkout and commit the updated patch.
  2. `offsetof_after_legacy_vis_t` above is a placeholder for the 80-byte
     offset called out in squeezelite/README.md.  In upstream this is either
     the tail of a locally-declared struct or a fixed constant depending on
     the branch — inspect the checkout and substitute the correct expression.
  3. The `n_stereo_frames` argument to `vis_shm_v1_end_write` must match the
     number of stereo frames just placed into the ring buffer.  Upstream
     tracks samples in scalar `s16` units in some code paths — divide by 2
     when handing the count to the v1 helper.

This file is not a machine-applicable patch; scripts/build-squeezelite.sh
still relies on it as documentation.  Automated regeneration against a fresh
upstream tree is the recommended workflow for producing a bit-exact patch.
